<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41513" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rē^tractĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		retraho. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A drawing back</i>, <i>retreating</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">graduum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the breadth</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					3, 4, 4</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A diminishing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dierum (opp. auctio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 14</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Hesitation</i>, <i>refusal</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sine ullā retractione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 162</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>